@baseUrl = http://localhost:5100

### Login with a synthetic user (Development/Testing)
# @name authLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "customer.demo",
  "password": "{{$processEnv Authentication__SeedPasswords__Customer}}"
}

### Refresh current session identity and CSRF token
# @name authMe
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

@csrfToken = {{authMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Startup readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Development OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Synthetic customer transactions (Development or Testing only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&transactionType=CardPurchase&fromDate=2026-11-01
X-Correlation-ID: demo-transaction-list

### Search owned descriptions, merchants and references before pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions?search=woolworths&pageSize=10

### Invalid query returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions?pageSize=101

### Cursor paging: copy pageInfo.nextCursor from the previous page (never combine with pageNumber)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions?pageSize=5

### Support contact details (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/support

### In-app notifications (customer), then mark all as read
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?limit=20

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/read
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### Owned synthetic transaction details (Development or Testing only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
X-Correlation-ID: demo-transaction-details

### Invalid transaction ID returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/not-a-guid

### Unknown or other-customer transaction returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099

### Evaluate owned transaction dispute eligibility (read-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/dispute-eligibility
X-Correlation-ID: demo-dispute-eligibility

### Valid DebiCheck: ordinary reversal blocked, authorization investigation remains available
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011/dispute-eligibility

### Registered Mandate (fixed collection date; window eligibility depends on current date)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000014/dispute-eligibility

### Mismatched DebiCheck amount requires investigation
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000023/dispute-eligibility

### Authorization complaint enters manual review only; repeat submission returns 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011",
  "reasonCode": "unauthorisedDebitOrder",
  "description": "I dispute the authorization recorded for this mandate."
}

### PR-15: send twice; the repeat returns the same case with Idempotent-Replayed: true.
# Change the description and resend with the same key to see 409 dispute.idempotencyKeyReused.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f1c2b7e-5d3a-4e8f-9a01-demo-retry-0001

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
  "reasonCode": "duplicateCharge",
  "description": "I was charged twice for the same purchase."
}

### Malformed eligibility transaction ID returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/not-a-guid/dispute-eligibility

### Unknown or other-customer eligibility transaction returns 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099/dispute-eligibility

### Unknown route returns Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/not-a-route

### PR-08: submit an eligible synthetic EFT dispute (repeat submission returns 409)
# @name debitOrderCase
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
  "reasonCode": "duplicateCollection",
  "description": "This collection needs investigation for a duplicate debit."
}

### Run sequentially, changing command to VerifyMandate, RequestReversal, ExecuteReversal, ReconcileReversal, Close
# Configure Simulation__DebitOrderKey in the API shell; REST Client must receive the same local value.
# Never commit the value or pass it to the customer frontend.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}/debit-order-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__DebitOrderKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: debit-order-demo
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "StartReview" }

### Use only after ExecuteReversal returns OutcomeUnknown; this queries MOCK-DO-{caseId} and never resubmits it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}/debit-order-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__DebitOrderKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: debit-order-reconcile
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "ReconcileReversal" }

### Ordinary customer processing is forbidden, even in Development
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}/debit-order-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "ExecuteReversal" }

### Read the customer-owned timeline without simulator privileges
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{debitOrderCase.response.body.$.id}}

### PR-09: submit a synthetic card case (repeat submission returns 409)
# @name cardCase
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "reasonCode": "duplicateCharge",
  "description": "This card purchase appears twice and needs investigation."
}

### Initiate, then ForwardToAcquirer, then MerchantAccept OR MerchantContest
# Configure Simulation__CardNetworkKey privately in the API and REST Client environments.
# MerchantAccept -> RequestSettlement -> ExecuteSettlement -> Close.
# MerchantContest -> ReceiveRepresentment (next example) -> ReviewRepresentment -> Approve OR Reject.
# Approve still requires RequestSettlement and ExecuteSettlement; Reject can Close without settlement.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{cardCase.response.body.$.id}}/chargeback-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__CardNetworkKey}}
X-Correlation-ID: card-chargeback-demo
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "Initiate" }

### Synthetic evidence metadata, only after MerchantContest; no file content is accepted
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{cardCase.response.body.$.id}}/chargeback-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__CardNetworkKey}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "command": "ReceiveRepresentment",
  "evidence": {
    "id": "aaaaaaaa-1111-4222-8333-444455556666",
    "kind": "Receipt"
  }
}

### Invalid jump (409 unless settlement was requested); repeating a processed operation also returns 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{cardCase.response.body.$.id}}/chargeback-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__CardNetworkKey}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "ExecuteSettlement" }

### Read separate chargeback, case, decision and financial statuses without the simulator key
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{cardCase.response.body.$.id}}

### PR-10: owned dispute dashboard (pageInfo.nextCursor is opaque; omit it on the first page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/disputes?pageSize=20

### Customer-safe chronological events, without simulator privileges
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/disputes/{{cardCase.response.body.$.id}}/events

### Submit an internal bank-fee complaint (repeat submission returns 409)
# @name bankFeeCase
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "transactionId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003",
  "reasonCode": "incorrectFee",
  "description": "Please investigate this bank fee and explain the charge."
}

### StartReview, then Approve, RequestAdjustment, ExecuteAdjustment, Close
# Alternatively StartReview, Reject, Close. Configure this private key in the API and REST Client environments.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/bank-charge-simulations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Simulation-Key: {{$processEnv Simulation__BankChargeKey}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "command": "StartReview" }

### Refresh case status and timeline; approval is not financial confirmation
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}

### Upload supporting evidence (PDF/PNG/JPEG up to 5 MB, 5 files per dispute); replace receipt.pdf locally
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/evidence
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ClearCaseBoundary

--ClearCaseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="note"

Statement showing the fee
--ClearCaseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="receipt.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./receipt.pdf
--ClearCaseBoundary--

### List evidence for the case (oldest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/evidence

### Withdraw an undecided dispute (409 dispute.withdrawalNotAllowed once decided, paid, escalated or charged back)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "expectedVersion": 1, "reason": "Resolved directly with the bank" }

### Logout requires the authenticated cookie and current CSRF token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### PR-29: sign in as an employee after customer logout; no simulation key
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "agent.demo",
  "password": "{{$processEnv Authentication__SeedPasswords__Agent}}"
}

### Refresh the employee CSRF token
# @name employeeMe
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

### Use a fresh bankFeeCase above; skip the preceding customer simulator commands
# @name employeeCase
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}

### Claim the case (workload only; 409 dispute.alreadyAssigned if someone else holds it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/assignment
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{employeeMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### List only my cases (assignment=mine|unassigned|all); items carry slaStatus and slaDueAt
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes?assignment=mine

### Release the assignment (assignee or Supervisor)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/assignment
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{employeeMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

### Read customer evidence (read-only); the detail response also lists financialOperations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/evidence

### Refresh employeeCase before each command: StartReview, Approve, RequestAdjustment, ExecuteAdjustment, Close
# Alternatively StartReview, Reject, Close. Approval alone never confirms funds.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/{{bankFeeCase.response.body.$.id}}/commands
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{employeeMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}
X-Correlation-ID: staff-case-command

{
  "command": "StartReview",
  "expectedVersion": {{employeeCase.response.body.$.version}}
}

### Repeating the previous request without refreshing employeeCase returns 409, not a second effect
### Unknown case returns 404; customer or anonymous sessions return 403 or 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/agent/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/commands
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{employeeMe.response.body.$.csrfToken}}

{ "command": "StartReview", "expectedVersion": 1 }